LaLog Compilation Project
=========================

Overview
--------

This repository contains an OCaml implementation of a small compiler pipeline
and a stack-based virtual machine.

The codebase is organized around two language families:

- `Expr`: a small expression language;
- `Pfx`: a stack-machine language and its virtual machine.

Each family has two variants:

- `basic`: the arithmetic-only version;
- `fun`: the extended version with functions, application, executable
  sequences, and closures.


Current Features
----------------

- `expr/basic`
  - arithmetic expressions with integers, variables, unary minus, and binary
    operators;
  - lexer, parser, and direct evaluator;
  - code generation to `basicPfx` for variable-free arithmetic expressions.
- `pfx/basic`
  - stack-machine instructions `push`, `pop`, `swap`, `add`, `sub`, `mul`,
    `div`, and `rem`;
  - lexer, parser, evaluator, and location-aware error reporting;
  - standalone lexer executable for token inspection.
- `expr/fun`
  - functions, application, and `let x = e1 in e2` syntactic sugar;
  - code generation to the extended `funPfx` machine.
- `pfx/fun`
  - executable sequences `( ... )`;
  - instructions `exec`, `get`, and `append`;
  - runtime support for closures.


Project Layout
--------------

Core directories:

- `utils`
  - shared location and error-reporting helpers.
- `expr/common`
  - shared binary-operator definitions.
- `expr/basic`
  - AST, lexer, parser, evaluator, and `Expr -> basicPfx` code generator.
- `expr/fun`
  - extended `Expr` frontend and `Expr -> funPfx` code generator.
- `pfx/basic`
  - basic stack machine, parser, evaluator, and standalone lexer driver.
- `pfx/fun`
  - extended stack machine with executable sequences and closures.

Top-level executables:

- `expr/main.exe`
  - evaluates a basic `Expr` file directly.
- `expr/compiler.exe`
  - compiles a basic `Expr` file to `basicPfx`, prints the generated program,
    then runs it.
- `expr/funCompiler.exe`
  - compiles an extended `Expr` file to `funPfx`, prints the generated
    program, then runs it.
- `pfx/pfxVM.exe`
  - parses and executes a basic `Pfx` program.
- `pfx/funVM.exe`
  - parses and executes an extended `Pfx` program.


Build
-----

Build everything with:

  dune build


Usage
-----

The simplest workflow is to build once, then run the generated binaries from
`_build/default`.

Evaluate a basic `Expr` program:

  ./_build/default/expr/main.exe expr/basic/tests/an_example.expr

Compile and run a basic `Expr` program through `basicPfx`:

  ./_build/default/expr/compiler.exe expr/basic/tests/an_example.expr

Parse and execute a basic `Pfx` program:

  ./_build/default/pfx/pfxVM.exe pfx/basic/tests/ok_prog.pfx

Inspect the token stream of a basic `Pfx` file:

  ./_build/default/pfx/basic/lexerStandalone.exe pfx/basic/tests/ok_prog.pfx

Compile and run extended `Expr` programs:

  ./_build/default/expr/funCompiler.exe expr/fun/tests/simple_app.expr
  ./_build/default/expr/funCompiler.exe expr/fun/tests/capture.expr
  ./_build/default/expr/funCompiler.exe expr/fun/tests/let_sugar.expr

Parse and execute extended `Pfx` programs:

  ./_build/default/pfx/funVM.exe pfx/fun/tests/ok_prog.pfx
  ./_build/default/pfx/funVM.exe pfx/fun/tests/exec_prog.pfx
  ./_build/default/pfx/funVM.exe pfx/fun/tests/get_prog.pfx
  ./_build/default/pfx/funVM.exe pfx/fun/tests/append_prog.pfx

Programs that expect stack arguments accept repeated `-a` options:

  ./_build/default/pfx/pfxVM.exe -a 7 -a 3 /tmp/args_prog.pfx


Representative Results
----------------------

The following commands currently work:

- `./_build/default/expr/main.exe expr/basic/tests/an_example.expr`
  prints `-67`.
- `./_build/default/expr/compiler.exe expr/basic/tests/an_example.expr`
  generates a `basicPfx` program and evaluates it to `-67`.
- `./_build/default/pfx/pfxVM.exe pfx/basic/tests/ok_prog.pfx`
  evaluates to `5`.
- `./_build/default/expr/funCompiler.exe expr/fun/tests/capture.expr`
  evaluates to `4`.
- `./_build/default/pfx/funVM.exe pfx/fun/tests/append_prog.pfx`
  evaluates to `6`.

